#TETHERVERSE FRONTEND — PRODUCTION
#
# Committed on purpose: every value here is a URL or a browser-visible origin, so
# there is no secret in this file, and a production config is worth reviewing in
# a diff.
#
# `pnpm build:worker` copies this file to `.env.production`, which is the name
# Next.js actually loads during a production build. Editing this file and
# building is therefore enough to change the deployed configuration.
#
# The name has to be exactly `.env.production`. Next.js reads a fixed list in
# production: `.env.production.local`, `.env.local`, `.env.production`, `.env`.
# A file called `.env.prod` is not on that list and is silently ignored, which
# would leave the build with none of these values and fall back to the
# development defaults baked into the source.
#
# ── Only build-time variables belong here ──────────────────────────────────
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the client bundle at build time, so
# changing one requires a rebuild and a redeploy. They belong in this file.
#
# TETHERVERSE_API_URL is NOT in this file, on purpose. It is not NEXT_PUBLIC_,
# so it is read at runtime from the Worker binding rather than inlined at build
# time — which is only true if it is absent from the build environment. Setting
# it here would bake the backend's address into the deployed bundle and make it
# unchangeable without a rebuild.
#
# On Workers it is a secret:
#
#   wrangler secret put TETHERVERSE_API_URL
#
#EXCEL PLAY AUTH CONFIG
NEXT_PUBLIC_EXCEL_AUTH_FRONTEND_URL=https://auth.excelmec.org
NEXT_PUBLIC_LAUNCHER_ORIGIN=https://play.excelmec.org
# Origins allowed to load the dev server. Empty in production: only the
# deployed Worker is meant to be loading this app.
ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=
